 "gaps": [
  "The model shows every element at its 2011 position. P6 flew on 4A in 2000 and sat atop Z1 until 10A relocated it in 2007, and PMA-2 and PMA-3 were also moved; the timeline shows each at its final place from launch.",
  "ceta: source LAYR names identify layer 3 as ceta B port and layer 4 as ceta A stbd. Per-part launch dates now distinguish STS-113 from STS-112; the grouped concept still starts on the first launch.",
  "obss: the reference guide's ULF6 entry names AMS and ELC-3; the boom was left on the station by the same flight (STS-134), per its cited mission page.",
  "esp1: the reference guide prints STS-98 beside 5A.1; the cited mission page gives STS-102, which is used here.",
  "mlm and era: the guide lists 3R without a date because it had not flown. Both launched in 2021, after the model's 2011 configuration, so the assembly timeline adds them only when it reaches complete."
 ]
